From: AOSC OS Packaging <packages@aosc.io>
Subject: [PATCH] add a loongarch64 target

Teach bun about loongarch64 so the AOSC OS LoongArch ports can build
natively.  A no-op on the architectures upstream releases.

Build system (scripts/build/):
- config.ts: the arch in the union, host detection ("loong64" is node's
  spelling), the derived boolean, the llvmArch triple for the sysroot cross
  path, and a `nosimd' knob for the SIMD-less port (Loongson 2K0300 class:
  no LSX/LASX, strict alignment) mirroring how `baseline' expresses the x64
  variant; tinycc defaults off -- it has no LoongArch code generator, so
  bun:ffi cc() degrades to dlopen-only exactly as upstream does on Android.
- build.ts: `nosimd' in the CLI boolean-field allowlist.
- flags.ts: -march=la64v1.0 -mtune=la664 per la-softdev-convention v0.2;
  nosimd takes -march=loongarch64 -msimd=none -mstrict-align.
- rust.ts: the triple mapping, an allRustTargets entry, and a direct
  spelling of the rustflags (-Ctarget-cpu=generic-la64 with +/-lsx) since
  the march-to-rustflags translation only parses x86 and armv8 grammar.
- deps/zlib.ts: generic C kernels satisfy the arch-exhaustive table (LSX
  kernels are a follow-up); deps/libjpeg-turbo.ts: WITH_SIMD stays
  undefined outside x64/arm64 (3.x guards every jsimd_* reference on it);
  deps/webkit.ts: no LoongArch MacroAssembler in JSC, so configure the
  CLoop interpreter instead of ENABLE_FTL_JIT (which would conflict), with
  USE_64KB_PAGE_BLOCK for the 16 KiB page kernels the port ships.

Sources:
- src/jsc/bindings/CPUFeatures.cpp: return no optional-feature bits
  instead of #error.
- src/windows_sys/externs.rs: teb()/peb() gain an unreachable!() arm --
  the crate has to type-check on every target it never runs on.
- src/bun_core/env.rs and the two exhaustive matches over Architecture
  (server_body.rs, compile_target.rs): a LoongArch64 variant, appended so
  the existing repr(u8) discriminants stay stable, spelled "loong64" the
  way node does.
- src/platform/linux.rs: a loongarch64 arm for raw_syscall6 (number in
  $a7, args in $a0..$a5, return in $a0, `syscall 0'; the kernel clobbers
  $t0-$t8, per musl's SYSCALL_CLOBBERLIST).
- src/crash_handler: an empty Flags/NAMED_FLAGS pair (bun_cpu_features()
  reports no optional bits here), and 'o' as the bun.report platform code
  -- not yet known to the decoder, avoids every code in use and the
  retired baseline ones.
- src/install_types/resolver_hooks.rs: a LOONG64 bit for the npm `cpu'
  field, spelled "loong64" as node does.
- patches/boringssl (new) + deps/boringssl.ts: target.h's supported-CPU
  allowlist ends in #error; BoringSSL's stated policy for other platforms is
  a local patch, so carry the three-line loongarch64 entry.
- patches/mimalloc (new) + deps/mimalloc.ts: mi_atomic_pause()'s final
  fallback spells identifiers that only exist in the MSVC-C branch of
  mimalloc's atomic.h; x86/arm/aarch64 all take the inline-asm arms above
  it, so loongarch64 is the first architecture to compile the fallback.
- C++ bindings vs a C_LOOP JSC: everything ENABLE(WEBASSEMBLY)-,
  ENABLE(JIT)- and ENABLE(SAMPLING_PROFILER)-shaped gains guards -- the
  GlobalObjectMethodTable streaming hooks (under !WEBASSEMBLY those two
  members become nameless void* placeholders, so positional tables pass
  nullptr and INHERIT_HOOK_METHOD cannot be used), the wasm-streaming
  cluster and JSWasmStreamingCompiler wrapper, NodeVM's eager JIT
  validation (the LLInt runs the code block as-is), the two
  SamplingProfiler-based CPU profilers (bun:jsc's profiler functions
  throw, Bun__stopCPUProfiler reports empty output), and the VM-init
  option block -- forcing useWasm on with no Wasm backend trips JSC's
  option-coherency abort.
- workaround-missing-symbols.cpp and the flags.ts --wrap list: the whole
  glibc-portability shim layer is compiled out on loongarch64 -- its
  glibc floor is 2.36, so none of the pre-2.3x compat symbols pinned
  there exist, and no pinning is needed.
- scripts/build/codegen.ts and src/js/node/os.ts: the bundler inlines
  `process.arch' into the builtin JS modules from a two-way table, so
  os.arch() on the port reported "arm64" and every consumer of it -- the
  build scripts' own host detection first of all -- picked ARM toolchain
  flags on LoongArch hardware; the endianness()/machine() branches also
  learn loong64, as their fallback arm is a bundle-time error.
- deps/zlib.ts sets WITH_ALL_FALLBACKS like the arm64 branch: off x86,
  functable's default path fills only part of the table and aborts at
  runtime with no arch kernels registered.
- Cargo.toml: the workspace hygiene denies (dead_code, unused_*,
  unreachable_*) demote to warnings.  On an architecture upstream does not
  build, helpers used only under other arches' cfg become dead code (e.g.
  bun_core/debug.rs PC_OFFSET), and each such deny is a build failure.

Signed-off-by: AOSC OS Packaging <packages@aosc.io>
